      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Statistics on the frequency of coronary insufficiency in patients with gout are contradictory. Nevertheless, it is shown that a correlation often exists between attacks of gout and attacks of angina or acute ischaemic episodes. Finally, these anatomo-clinical studies prove the reality of the gouty heart if only because of the discovery of deposits of intracardiac urates."},
